{"id":"e02t1","name":"Latest Warehouse Snapshots","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A logistics company runs several warehouses. Every night, each warehouse uploads a stock snapshot as a CSV file. The files are stored in <code>input_dir</code> with this layout:</p>\n<pre class=\"exv\">input_dir/\n  &lt;warehouse&gt;/\n    &lt;YYYYMMDD&gt;.csv</pre>\n<p>For example <code>input_dir/casa_north/20260302.csv</code> is the snapshot of warehouse <code>casa_north</code> on 2 March 2026. A warehouse folder can contain several snapshots.</p>\n<p>Every file has a header line and the three columns <code>sku</code>, <code>qty</code> and <code>location</code>. <b>Each warehouse exports the columns in its own order</b> (for example <code>qty,sku,location</code>), and header names can contain spaces and capital letters. Values are also messy:</p>\n<ul><li><code>sku</code> can have surrounding spaces and lower-case letters; SKUs are compared after trimming and upper-casing;</li><li><code>qty</code> is an integer written as text; an empty, non-numeric or negative quantity counts as <code>0</code>;</li><li>the same SKU can appear on several lines of one file (several locations): its quantity is the sum of these lines.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return, for each warehouse, the stock of its <b>latest</b> snapshot only, with the columns <code>warehouse</code>, <code>sku</code>, <code>qty</code> (integer) and <code>snapshot_date</code> (date), sorted by <code>warehouse</code>, then <code>sku</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/casa_north/20260301.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">sku,qty,location\nA-1,10,R1\nB-2,4,R2\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/casa_north/20260302.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">sku,qty,location\nA-1,8,R1\nc-3 ,,R3\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/rabat/20260302.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\"> QTY , SKU , LOCATION \n5,a-7,S1\n2, A-7,S2\nx,B-2,S1\n</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>warehouse</th><th>sku</th><th>qty</th><th>snapshot_date</th></tr><tr><td>casa_north</td><td>A-1</td><td>8</td><td>2026-03-02</td></tr><tr><td>casa_north</td><td>C-3</td><td>0</td><td>2026-03-02</td></tr><tr><td>rabat</td><td>A-7</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02</td></tr><tr><td>rabat</td><td>B-2</td><td>0</td><td>2026-03-02</td></tr></table></div>\n<p><code>casa_north</code> has two snapshots: only <code>20260302.csv</code> is used. In <code>rabat</code>, the columns come in another order, <code>a-7</code> appears twice (<code>5 + 2</code>) and <code>\"x\"</code> counts as <code>0</code>.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"import os\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return spark.read.option(\"header\", True).csv(input_dir)\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["lire un dossier","os.walk","unionByName","colonnes dans le désordre"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"casa_north/20260301.csv":"sku,qty,location\nA-1,10,R1\nB-2,4,R2\n","casa_north/20260302.csv":"sku,qty,location\nA-1,8,R1\nc-3 ,,R3\n","rabat/20260302.csv":" QTY , SKU , LOCATION \n5,a-7,S1\n2, A-7,S2\nx,B-2,S1\n"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"casa_north/20260301.csv":"sku,qty,location\nA-1,10,R1\nB-2,4,R2\n","casa_north/20260302.csv":"sku,qty,location\nA-1,8,R1\nc-3 ,,R3\n","rabat/20260302.csv":" QTY , SKU , LOCATION \n5,a-7,S1\n2, A-7,S2\nx,B-2,S1\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["warehouse","sku","qty","snapshot_date"],"rows":[["casa_north","A-1",8,"2026-03-02"],["casa_north","C-3",0,"2026-03-02"],["rabat","A-7",7,"2026-03-02"],["rabat","B-2",0,"2026-03-02"]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"fes/20260228.csv":" LOCATION , SKU , QTY \nL1,Z-9,-3\nL1,Y-1,12\n","fes/20260227.csv":"location,qty,sku\nL1,100,Z-9\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["warehouse","sku","qty","snapshot_date"],"rows":[["fes","Y-1",12,"2026-02-28"],["fes","Z-9",0,"2026-02-28"]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}